Speech for the Handover Session
Good morning everyone,
Thank you for joining this handover and UAT2 working session.
The objective of today's session is to walk through the Market Value reconciliation process that we use to support LAM reporting validation in Murex. In particular, I would like to explain how this reconciliation underpins the validation of P&L Summary, P&L VaR, and P&L Attribution, and to ensure that the team has a clear understanding of the methodology, controls, and current open issues before proceeding with UAT2 sign-off activities. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
I will start by providing some context on the role of Market Value reconciliation within the broader UAT2 testing effort. The reconciliation serves as a critical control to verify that positions, valuations, and aggregations are consistent between Murex and our reference production sources before we analyze reporting outputs. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
Next, I will present the end-to-end reconciliation process, including the source data extracted from Murex and Summit, the controls applied to the data, and the various reconciliation levels we perform—from trade and security level all the way up to sub-account, portfolio, and book aggregation. The purpose is not only to identify differences, but also to understand the drivers behind those differences and determine whether they are expected, explainable, or require remediation. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
I will then demonstrate how this reconciliation feeds directly into the validation of our reporting outputs. For the P&L Summary, it helps confirm that valuations and positions are correctly reflected at the portfolio and sub-account levels. For P&L VaR and P&L Attribution, it provides confidence that the underlying market values used in the analysis are accurate and comparable across systems. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
As part of the handover, I will also review the main observations identified so far. We have encountered several differences related to currency conversion, clean versus dirty price treatment, accrual methodology, settlement treatment, and other data-quality issues. Some of these items have already been analyzed, while others are being tracked through TFS and require further investigation. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
One of the key messages I would like everyone to take away from this session is that the reconciliation process is not simply a control exercise. It is the foundation for understanding and explaining the differences we observe in P&L reporting and for ensuring confidence in the future-state Murex reporting framework.
Finally, we will discuss the remaining UAT2 activities, the evidence required for sign-off, ownership of open items, and the next steps needed to close outstanding gaps. My goal is that, by the end of this session, everyone understands the process, knows where the current issues stand, and is aligned on the actions required to move forward. [UAT2 Worki...Reporting | Meeting]
Thank you, and let's begin with a brief overview of the reconciliation framework before moving into the detailed walkthrough.